This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: If you apply a greased figurine or stone-to-flesh a greased
statue, it should become a greased monster. This would make the monster
slippery and fast! "Your greased mumak called Whiskers moves like
greased lightning!" - azgor

[2]: Any coaligned unattended altar should become sanctuary for a
priest character upon entering the room. - jmr

[3]: Either the HoOA should have no effect on neutrals other than
welding to your head (strict interpretation of "opposite") or it should
have a chance of making you neutral if you are Law or Cha (loose
interpretation). Say, 20% or so. As it stands, the only way to use
neutral artifacts is to start as neutral. That seems imbalanced in
favor of neutral roles. - azgor

[4]: Sitting on gold should be comfortable, and exercise charisma, when
polymorphed into a dragon. - SpeedEvil

[5]: Since it is well known that early religious practices of some
tribes used hallucinatory drugs as a means to dealing with the divine,
taking a hallucinogen should give you temporary telepathy or
clairvoyance if you are a caveman. - aristotle73

[6]: There should be a chance of losing worn rings down a sink when you
quaff from one. -azgor

[7]: a magic marker should work like a ?oScare Monster for paper golems
(how about a scroll of fire? -ed.) - braindancer

[8]: Blessing a blessed item/cursing a cursed item should yield a(n
un)holy item, altering its characteristics further where applicable.
Water could only be blessed or cursed once, of course. - Grunt

[9]: Giants should be able to eat items made of bone as per "I'll grind
his bones to make my bread" from 'Jack and the Beanstalk' - azgor

[10]: One mumak is to mumakil as a mimic should be to mimicid.  :)  And
genociding mimics should further be known as mimicide. - Grunt

[11]: You should be able to foo-proof any foo-proofable non-armor item
by wielding it and reading ?oEW while confused.  This would allow you
to make fireproof scrolls, not just wish for them. - azgor

[12]: Rust, fire damage, rot and corrosion should affect wands and
jewelry by making their effects intermittent. This could make it
worthwhile to fooproof these items. - azgor

[13]: You should be able to attach a bell to a pet kitten/cat. This
would cause monsters to be aggravated by the cat and be less likely to
attack you. -azgor

[14]: Multilevel stores. - moussambani

[15]: Breaking a wand should do damage proportional to charges+1
instead of to charges because of the wrestable charge in a seemingly
empty wand. - azgor

Individual ideas may have contributions from multiple authors/editors,
